        "original_id": "6b94197b-8a5d-5d0f-ae32-38f19fab0440",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dean Jones, Laurens van der Post\n- Films and TV series: The Million Dollar Duck, The $1,000,000 Duck, A Far Off Place, Ensign O'Toole, The Love Bug, Beethoven\n- Companies and networks: Walt Disney Productions, NBC\n- Roles and works: Jim Douglas, Albert Dooley, Dr. Herman Varnick, A Far-Off Place, A Story Like the Wind\n\nFacts:\n- Ensign O'Toole aired on NBC from September 23, 1962, to May 5, 1963, as a military comedy series.\n- Dean Jones, then age 31, played the title role in Ensign O'Toole as a nonchalant United States Navy ensign.\n- The Love Bug was released in 1968, and Dean Jones played Jim Douglas in it.\n- The Million Dollar Duck, also titled The $1,000,000 Duck, is a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a goose that lays golden eggs.\n- Dean Jones played Albert Dooley in The Million Dollar Duck in 1971 and received a Golden Globe nomination for that role.\n- A Story Like the Wind was published in 1972, and A Far-Off Place was published in 1974 as works by Laurens van der Post.\n- A Far Off Place is a 1993 American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works A Far-Off Place and A Story Like the Wind.\n- Beethoven was released in 1992, and Dean Jones played Dr. Herman Varnick in it.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "de1041c9-d0f7-5c46-a99e-220aa1986330",
        "text": "Page: The Million Dollar Duck. Sentence: The Million Dollar Duck (also titled as The $1,000,000 Duck) is a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions about a goose that lays golden eggs scenario.\nPage: A Far Off Place. Sentence: A Far Off Place is a 1993 American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works \"A Far-Off Place\" (1974) and its prequel \"A Story Like the Wind\" (1972).\nPage: Dean Jones (actor). Sentence: \" (1965), Jim Douglas in \"The Love Bug\" (1968), Albert Dooley in \"The Million Dollar Duck\" (1971; for which he received a Golden Globe nomination) and Dr. Herman Varnick in \"Beethoven\" (1992).\nPage: Ensign O'Toole. Sentence: Ensign O'Toole is a military comedy that aired on NBC from September 23, 1962, to May 5, 1963, with 31-year-old Dean Jones in the title role of a nonchalant United States Navy ensign during the early 1960s.",
